What is a Server?
A Server is a computer (or machine) that provides services, data, or resources to other computers (clients).
A server mainly consists of:
Operating System (OS)
RAM
Processor (CPU)
Storage
Network Connection
Whenever a client sends a request, the server processes it and returns a response.
Client  --->  Server  --->  Response
Real-Life Example
Imagine you search for Headphones on Amazon.
What happens?
You search for "Headphones".
Your request goes to Amazon's server.
The server searches its database.
It finds all related headphones.
The server sends the result back to you.
User
   |
Search "Headphones"
   |
Internet
   |
Amazon Server
   |
Database Search
   |
Response
   |
List of Headphones
